A||||3||Ozzy||'88 coupe electrical problems...
Z||000000||Ozzy||08-22-99||10:21 PM||||Got a weird electrical problem going on. If anyone has had a similar problem please let me know.<p>Started with the backup power on the radio. (stock factory) When I open either door and the door switch closes the backup power to the radio dissapears. Also the the same thing with the cigar lighter. I checked with a VOM and the voltage is 0vdc at the radio and cigar lighter. Also the horn has stopped working and the courtesy lights. When I try to work the horn, there is a buzz and the courtesy lights glow dimmly. The car does have after market steering wheel and air horns. Horn was working before.<p>In the Haynes manual I have the electrical schematics show unswitched power feeding on the same circuit to the horn, cigar lighter, radio backup and courtesy lights. I don't figure it is a ground problem because I would expect to see some voltage at the lighter as opposed to 0.<p>Ozzy
Z||000001||DJRice||08-23-99||08:16 AM||||If you have a short, (ie something grounded out) you likely wont read much more than zero.  With the door open, the courtesy lights should come on, which is why you have a problem when you open a door.  <p>There is a connector behind the area where your fuse box is located, mounted up on the frame of the car.  This connects the courtesy lights up to the system.  However, it is more likely that if someone has replaced the horn with something different, then the horn wiring could be the problem.  I would look at the wiring for that first, because that is more likely to be the problem, because it has been played with. <p>Good luck....
Z||000002||theogre||08-23-99||11:41 AM||||check the thin wires comming off the batery. They will cause this kind of thing.
Z||000003||Ozzy||08-24-99||09:10 AM||||BrB!!!  It helps if u check da fuse!!!<p>I can't believe that the other electrical stuff was happening. It threw me completley.<p>All is well<p>Ozzy
